{"name":"Welsh Onion","hex":"#22bb66","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"welsh","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cheat or swindle someone, often by not paying a debt, especially a gambling debt.","To go back on one's word."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Foreign."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/welsh"},{"term":"onion","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A monocotyledonous plant (Allium cepa), allied to garlic, used as vegetable and spice.","The bulb of such a plant."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/onion"}],"entries":[{"title":"Allium fistulosum","blocks":[{"text":"Allium fistulosum, the Welsh onion, also commonly called Japanese bunching onion, stone-leek, and spring onion, is a species of perennial plant, often considered to be a kind of scallion."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Welsh_onion.jpg/330px-Welsh_onion.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Allium_fistulosum"},{"title":"Onion","blocks":[{"text":"The onion, also known as the bulb onion or common onion, is a vegetable that is the most widely cultivated species of the genus Allium. The shallot is a botanical variety of the onion which was classified as a separate species until 2011. The onion's close relatives include garlic, scallion, leek, and chives."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Mixed_onions.jpg/330px-Mixed_onions.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Onion"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Scallion_2.png/500px-Scallion_2.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Scallion_2.png/1280px-Scallion_2.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=th